{
  "title": "Scapholunate Ligament Injury & DISI",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6041/scapholunate-ligament-injury-and-disi",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 9 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Scapholunate Ligament Injury is a source of dorsoradial wrist pain with chronic injuries leading to a form of wrist instability (DISI deformity).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with PA wrist radiographs showing widening of the SL joint. Diagnosis of DISI deformity can be made with lateral wrist radiographs showing a scapholunate angle > 70 degrees.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment of acute SL ligament injuries may be immobilization versus operative repair/reconstruction depending on degree of displacement. Chronic DISI deformities may be indicated for fusion procedures depending on degree of arthritis and patient symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "acute injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs in approximately **10-30%** of intra-articular distal radius fractures or carpal fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "degenerative injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "degenerative tears in **>50%** of people over the age of 80 years old",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ligament has **3 components** that span between the scaphoid and lunate bones",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**dorsal, proximal and volar components**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "incomplete tears > complete tears",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "sudden impact force applied to the hand and wrist causing SLIL injury and scapholunate dissociation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**injury occurs most commonly with wrist positioned in extension, ulnar deviation and carpal supination**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "osseous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "SLIL tearing will position the scaphoid in flexion and lunate extension",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "ligamentous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "diastasis of the scapholunate complex occurs with complete SLIL tears and capsule disruption.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**DISI (dorsal intercalated segmental instability)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "scapholunate dissociation causes the scaphoid to flex palmar and the lunate to dorsiflex",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "if left untreated the DISI deformity can progress into a **SLAC wrist**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "DISI deformity may also develop secondary to distal pole of the scaphoid excision for treatment of STT arthritis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "DISI is a form of carpal instability dissociative",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Scapholunate interosseous ligament**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "location",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "c-shaped structure connecting the dorsal, proximal and volar surfaces of the scaphoid and lunate bones",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "dorsal fibers thickened (3 mm) compared to volar fibers (1 mm) and considered most important for stability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "biomechanics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**dorsal component provides the greatest constraint to translation between the scaphoid and lunate bones**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**proximal fibers have minimal mechanical strength**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Overview of wrist ligaments and biomechanics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**acute FOOSH injury vs. degenerative rupture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "age, nature of injury, duration since injury, degree of underlying arthritis, level of activity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually **dorsal and radial-sided wrist pain**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain increased with loading across the wrist (e.g. push up position)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "clicking or catching in the wrist",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may be associated with wrist instability or weakness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may see swelling over the dorsal aspect of the wrist",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tenderness in the anatomical snuffbox or over the **dorsal scapholunate interval** (just distal to Lister's tubercle)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain increased with extreme wrist extension and radial deviation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Watson test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "when deviating from ulnar to radial, pressure over volar aspect of scaphoid subluxates the scaphoid dorsally out of the scaphoid fossa of the distal radius, and a clunk is palpated when pressure is released as the scaphoid reduces back over the dorsal rim of the radius",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "a painful clunk during this maneuver may indicate insufficiency of scapholunate ligament",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral views of the wrist",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "additional views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "radial and ulnar deviation views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flexion and extension views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "clenched fist (can exaggerate the diastasis)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**SL gap > 3mm** with **clenched fist view** (Terry Thomas sign)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6041/images/reivew%20clenched%20fist.jpg",
                          "caption": "Scapho-lunate widening on PA clenched fist view"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**cortical ring sign** (caused by scaphoid malalignment)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6041/images/DISI%20-%20AP%20-%20Terry%20Thomas%20sign%20and%20cortical%20ring_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**humpback deformity** with DISI associated with an unstable scaphoid fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**scaphoid shortening**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Lateral radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**dorsal tilt of lunate leads to SL angle > 70°** on neutral rotation lateral",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6041/images/DISI%20-%20lateral_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "capitolunate angle > 20°",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "DISI",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "normal carpal alignment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6041/images/gw300h551..jpg",
                          "caption": "Normal alignment"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "increased SL angle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6041/images/gw275h550..jpg",
                          "caption": "DISI"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Arthrography",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be used as screening tool for arthroscopy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "radiocarpal and midcarpal views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "always assess the contralateral wrist for comparison",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may demonstrate the presence of a tear but cannot determine the size of the tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "positive finding of a tear may indicate the need for wrist arthroscopy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often overused as a screening modality for SLIL tears",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "requires careful inspection of the SLIL by a dedicated radiologist to confirm diagnosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "low sensitivity for tears",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Arthroscopy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "considered the **gold standard for diagnosis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "LT ligament injury & VISI deformity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Carpal instability nondissociative (CIND)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDS, rest +/- immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "acute, undisplaced SLIL injuries",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "chronic, asymptomatic tears",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "splinting and close follow-up with repeat imaging and clinical response with acute injuries",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most people feel casting alone is insufficient",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "may be effective with incomplete tears",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "scapholunate ligament repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "acute scapholunate ligament injury without carpal malalignment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "chronic but **reducible** scapholunate ligament injuries (can peform if < 18 months from the time of injury)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ligament pathoanatomy is ammenable to repair",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "scapholunate reconstruction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**acute** scapholunate ligament injury without carpal malalignment where pathoanatomy is not ammenable to repair",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**reducible** scapholunate ligament injuries > 18 months from the time of injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "scaphoid ORIF vs. CRPP (+/- arthroscopic assistance)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if pathoanatomy of SL ligament injury is a scaphoid fx than repair with **ORIF vs. CRPP** (+/- arthroscopic assistance)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "stabilization with wrist fusion (STT or SLC)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**rigid and unreducible DISI deformity**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "DISI with severe DJD",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "scaphotrapezialtrapezoidal (STT) fusion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "scapholunocapitate (SLC) fusion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "scapholunate fusion alone has **highest nonunion rate**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Scapholunate ligament direct repair SLIL with k-wires**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "small incision is made just distal to the radial styloid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "care to avoid cutting the radial sensory nerve branches",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "methods",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "SL joint pinning with k-wires",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "suture anchors with k-wires",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Blatt dorsal capsulodesis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "often added to a ligament repair and remains a viable alternative for a chronic instability when ligament repair is not feasible",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "repair technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "place two k-wires in parallel into the scaphoid bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "reduce the SL joint by levering the scaphoid into extension, supination and ulnar deviation and lunate into flexion and radial deviation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pass the k wires into the lunate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "confirm reduction of the SL joint under fluoroscopy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "place patient in short arm cast",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "post-operative care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "remove k-wires in 8-10 weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "no heavy labor for 4-6 months",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Scapholunate ligament reconstruction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "same as for repair",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reconstruction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "FCR tendon transfer (direct SL joint reduction)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ECRB tendonosis (indirect SL joint reduction)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "weave not recommended due to high incidence of late failure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
